column2:
Homage to the dweller in Dvaraka, the dweller in the forest of tulsi; homage to Padmanabha; homage to you, lotus-footed.
naradapuran:156:33	Homage to the lotus-handed, lotus-eyed; protector of Kamala (Lakshmi), homage, homage to Keshava.
naradapuran:156:34	Homage to the sun-formed, bearer of the moon-form; to the one in the form of the guardians of the world, bearing the body of Prajapati;
naradapuran:156:35	to the form of the host of beings, to the form of the soul, to radiance; to Victory, the victor, the leader, to discipline, the nature of action;
naradapuran:156:36	to the one without qualities, without effort, expert in policy, whose nature is non-action; to the Buddha, to the Kalki-form, the knower of the field, the imperishable;
naradapuran:156:37	to Govinda, the sustainer of the world, the infinite, the primal, the bearer of the Sharnga bow; to the conch-bearer, mace-bearer, and to the discus-bearer, homage;
naradapuran:156:38	to the sword-bearer, trident-bearer, destroyer of all weapons and missiles; to the refuge, the choicest, the highest, the Supreme Self;
naradapuran:156:39	to Hrishikesha, to the universe, to the universal form, homage to you; to the one with navel of time, to Time, to the sun and moon as eyes, homage; to the full, to be served, higher than the highest,
naradapuran:156:40	to the maker of the world, sustainer of the world, ordainer of the world, ender; to the bewilderer, agitator, assumer of desired forms, unborn, wise —
naradapuran:156:41	Lord, we have come to you for refuge, tormented by demons; do for us, support of all, so that we may be happy,
naradapuran:156:42	and live with sons, friends, wives and the rest. Hearing their hymn, Vaikuntha, pleased in mind,
